<title>NETHERLANDS: Shell's Wavin first-half net up 35 percent.</title>
<headline>Shell's Wavin first-half net up 35 percent.</headline>
<dateline>ZWOLLE, Netherlands 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996 (in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    19.8  vs  14.7</p>
<p>    Turnover (billions)		  0.86 vs   1.04</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    58.5  vs  55.0</p>
<p>    Cash flow			     70.4  vs  69.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Plastics maker Wavin BV, which is 50 percent owned by Royal Dutch/Shell, said it expected a 1996 full-year profit increase in line with the first-half trend and added it saw a further increase in 1997 and beyond.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
